            <ArticleTitle>Gas in a spinal extradural cyst. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes a patient with sciatica resulting from lumbar root compression by a gas-containing cyst in the extradural space. Removal of the cyst provided prompt relief. The origin and anatomic distribution of gas collections in the spine are considered based on a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
